        // face. That centering is exactly what makes a FROZEN (scrollable)
        // word look "cut off at the top": centering splits the overflow
        // evenly above and below the box, and the half that lands above
        // the box's own top edge is also above the scrollable area's top —
        // no amount of scrolling down can ever reach it, since there's
        // nothing to scroll UP into. Forcing these ancestors to flex-start
